// The Lectern. From The Floor (Verbal Authority Practice, 2026).
window.LECTERN_FLOOR={"directness":[{"id":"fl-dir-1","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I've made the call. We're moving the showcase to the second week.","land":"made","note":"No 'I think we should probably'. The decision is already past tense."},{"id":"fl-dir-2","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That won't work, and here's what will.","land":"won","note":"Land: 'won't'. Pair every no with the alternative in the same breath. It reads as leadership, not obstruction."},{"id":"fl-dir-3","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let me be clear about what I need from this meeting.","land":"clear","note":"Then stop. State the one thing. Don't soften it with a second thing."},{"id":"fl-dir-4","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I hear the concern. My answer is still no.","land":"still","note":"Acknowledgement is not agreement. You can do both in one sentence."},{"id":"fl-dir-5","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"We're not relitigating this. The decision stands.","land":"stands","note":"Short sentences carry more weight than long ones. Resist the urge to explain twice."},{"id":"fl-dir-6","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Here's where I land on it.","land":"land","note":"Opens an opinion with authority instead of 'I sort of feel like maybe'."},{"id":"fl-dir-7","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'll have it to you by Friday. Not before, and not late.","land":"Friday","note":"Specificity is authority. A vague commitment sounds like an apology in advance."},{"id":"fl-dir-8","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Two things. First, the budget. Second, the timeline.","land":"Two","note":"Signposting numbers stops you rambling and tells the room exactly how long you'll take."},{"id":"fl-dir-9","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I don't have that yet. I'll know by Thursday.","land":"yet","note":"'I don't know' with a deadline attached is confidence. 'I don't know' alone is not."},{"id":"fl-dir-10","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let's name the actual problem before we solve the wrong one.","land":"actual","note":"Reframes the room without putting anyone down. Slows a meeting that's spiralling."},{"id":"fl-dir-11","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'd rather get this right than get it fast.","land":"right","note":"A clean trade-off stated out loud ends the pressure to rush."},{"id":"fl-dir-12","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's a separate conversation. Let's finish this one first.","land":"separate","note":"Protects the agenda without dismissing the person."},{"id":"fl-dir-13","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I want one decision out of this meeting. Here it is.","land":"one","note":"Naming the outcome up front stops a meeting drifting into a discussion with no end."},{"id":"fl-dir-14","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"No. And I'm comfortable with that.","land":"comfortable","note":"A no you don't defend is stronger than a no you over-explain."},{"id":"fl-dir-15","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let's not confuse activity with progress here.","land":"progress","note":"Cuts through a room that's busy doing the wrong thing."},{"id":"fl-dir-16","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'll take that on. You can stop worrying about it.","land":"take","note":"Claiming ownership cleanly is more reassuring than ten words of reassurance."},{"id":"fl-dir-17","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"What would have to be true for this to work?","land":"true","note":"Turns a vague objection into a concrete test. Reframes without conflict."},{"id":"fl-dir-18","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I disagree, and I'd like to say why.","land":"disagree","note":"Stated plainly and early, it carries far more than a buried 'I'm not sure I fully agree'."},{"id":"fl-dir-19","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's not the question. The question is whether we can staff it.","land":"question","note":"Redirects a meeting to the thing that actually decides the outcome."},{"id":"fl-dir-20","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I need a yes or no on this by end of day.","land":"yes or no","note":"Closing off the middle ground forces a decision instead of a maybe."},{"id":"fl-dir-21","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let me finish the thought.","land":"finish","note":"Four words, said calmly, reclaim the floor without raising your voice."},{"id":"fl-dir-22","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's a fair point. It doesn't change my recommendation.","land":"doesn","note":"Land: 'doesn't'. You can fully grant a point and still hold your position. Both, in one breath."},{"id":"fl-dir-23","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Here's what I'm certain of, and here's what I'm still weighing.","land":"certain","note":"Separating the two openly is more authoritative than pretending you're sure of everything."},{"id":"fl-dir-24","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"We've talked about this enough. Time to decide.","land":"decide","note":"A clean call to close is leadership. Endless discussion is not."},{"id":"fl-dir-25","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'm going to push back on that.","land":"push","note":"Announcing the disagreement before you make it reads as confident, not combative."},{"id":"fl-dir-26","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"The short answer is no. The longer answer is also no, with reasons.","land":"short","note":"A touch of dry humour can carry a firm no without hardening the room."},{"id":"fl-dir-27","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's outside what I can commit to right now.","land":"commit","note":"Names the limit without apology or a long excuse."},{"id":"fl-dir-28","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let's be honest about what this will actually cost us.","land":"actually","note":"Invites the room into a real conversation instead of a comfortable one."},{"id":"fl-dir-29","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I've heard everyone. Here's the call.","land":"call","note":"Signals that listening is done and a decision is coming. The room settles."},{"id":"fl-dir-30","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's a maybe from me, and I want to be straight that it's a maybe.","land":"straight","note":"Owning an honest uncertainty is stronger than faking a yes you'll walk back."},{"id":"fl-dir-31","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let's park that and come back to it with fresh eyes.","land":"park","note":"Defers cleanly without letting a tangent kill the meeting."},{"id":"fl-dir-32","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'm not going to pretend that's fine. It isn't.","land":"isn","note":"Land: 'isn't'. Naming a problem directly is the first move of someone who intends to fix it."},{"id":"fl-dir-33","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Give me the headline first, then the detail.","land":"headline","note":"Directs how someone reports to you. Trains the room to lead with what matters."},{"id":"fl-dir-34","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That decision's mine to make, and I've made it.","land":"mine","note":"Claims the authority that's actually yours, without aggression."},{"id":"fl-dir-35","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I want to slow this down for a second.","land":"slow","note":"Deliberately decelerating a rushed room is a quiet form of control."},{"id":"fl-dir-36","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"Let's agree on the problem before we argue about the answer.","land":"problem","note":"Stops two people solving different things at each other."},{"id":"fl-dir-37","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'll own that mistake. Here's how I'm fixing it.","land":"own","note":"Taking a clean hit and pivoting straight to the fix is authority, not weakness."},{"id":"fl-dir-38","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"What's the one thing that has to happen this week?","land":"one","note":"Forces a sprawling agenda down to a single priority."},{"id":"fl-dir-39","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"I'd like us to decide, not just discuss.","land":"decide","note":"Names the difference out loud and moves the room toward a close."},{"id":"fl-dir-40","family":"Directness","cue":"","say":"That's enough detail. I trust you to handle the rest.","land":"trust","note":"Cutting off over-explanation and handing back ownership reads as confidence in both directions."}],"interventions":[{"id":"fl-int-1","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Open","say":"Before we get into the detail, I want to *separate* two things. | There's the substantive question of whether the program belongs in the faculty at all, | and there's the procedural question of who decides. | I think we'll move faster if we settle the first *before* we touch the second.","note":"Why it lands: the substantive-versus-procedural split is pure governance fluency, and opening by structuring the conversation quietly puts you in charge of it without claiming the chair. The pause after 'all' lets the distinction sink in."},{"id":"fl-int-2","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Challenge","say":"Can I *test* that a little. | The proposal reads well on paper, but it rests on enrolments holding steady, | and everything we've seen this year points the other way. | I'm not against the direction. I'd want the assumption made *explicit* before we commit to it.","note":"Why it lands: 'test' frames disagreement as rigour, not opposition. Naming the load-bearing assumption is the senior move – you're not rejecting the case, you're finding the one beam holding it up. The short 'I'm not against the direction' keeps the relationship intact."},{"id":"fl-int-3","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"On the spot","say":"That's a fair question, and I'm going to *take it on notice* rather than give you half an answer now. | I'd rather come back next meeting with something I can stand behind | than commit us to a figure I'd have to walk back.","note":"Why it lands: 'take it on notice' is the formal, unembarrassed way to not answer under pressure. It reads as discipline, not evasion. The reason you give – not wanting to walk something back – frames the deferral as integrity. This is your single best defence against the stumble."},{"id":"fl-int-4","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Close","say":"Let me say back what I think we've *landed* on, so we're not relitigating it next month. | We're agreed in principle, | the working group takes the detail, | and it comes back here for ratification in the cyclical review. | Have I got that right?","note":"Why it lands: summarising at the end quietly hands you authorship of the outcome. 'Ratification' and 'cyclical review' are exact governance terms. Ending on 'Have I got that right' is generous – it invites correction, which is what makes the summary trustworthy rather than a power grab."},{"id":"fl-int-5","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Build","say":"I want to *build* on what Penelope said, because I think it's the crux and it's at risk of getting lost. | Her point about staged implementation isn't a side issue – | it's the difference between this working and this collapsing in term one.","note":"Why it lands: this is intelligent agreement done right. You're not praising her to look gracious, you're elevating a point because it's genuinely the crux, and in doing so you demonstrate judgement. Respect follows from being the person who saw what mattered."},{"id":"fl-int-6","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Open","say":"I'd start by reminding us this is *consensus* advice, not a vote, | so my aim isn't to win the point – it's to find the position we can all put our names to. | On that basis, here's where I think the difficulty actually sits.","note":"Why it lands: naming the committee's actual mode of operation marks you as someone inside the work. Reframing your own goal as consensus rather than victory is disarming and senior. It earns you the floor for the harder thing you say next."},{"id":"fl-int-7","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'd want to be careful here. | The proposal lifts the content but it doesn't lift the *achievement standards* to match, | and that mismatch is exactly the kind of thing that erodes comparability between schools. | I don't think we can advise on it until that's reconciled.","note":"Why it lands: holding content and achievement standards apart is the tell of genuine SCSA fluency – conflating them marks an outsider. 'Comparability between schools' invokes a real equity principle the body is bound to protect, so your objection isn't personal, it's structural."},{"id":"fl-int-8","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"On the spot","say":"Honestly, I don't have the *evidence base* for that in front of me, | and I'd rather say so than guess. | What I can tell you is what I'd want to see before forming a view – | the moderation data across at least three cohorts.","note":"Why it lands: admitting you don't have the evidence, then immediately naming exactly what evidence would settle it, converts a gap into a demonstration of rigour. You look more credible for not bluffing, and you've quietly set the terms of the next discussion."},{"id":"fl-int-9","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Close","say":"So if I'm reading the room, | we're comfortable with the direction, | the concern is the *implementation timeline*, | and we'd want schools given proper lead time for professional learning. | I'd suggest we frame our advice exactly that way.","note":"Why it lands: 'if I'm reading the room' is a softer, equally authoritative version of summarising. Moving the debate from whether to when-and-how is where the real risk usually lives, and being the one to name it is the contribution that earns standing."},{"id":"fl-int-10","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Build","say":"I think David's put his finger on it, | and I'd just sharpen it slightly. | The issue isn't the syllabus content – that's sound – | it's whether it's *fit for purpose* in a small-cohort school, which is a different question entirely.","note":"Why it lands: 'sharpen it slightly' is the move – you agree, then add the precision that makes the point usable. Granting that the content is sound before raising the real concern shows you're fair-minded, which makes the concern land harder."},{"id":"fl-int-11","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Open","say":"Before we go further, I'd ask one question. | Is this a matter of *governance*, or is it operational? | Because if it's operational, we'd be straying into management by deciding it here, | and I don't think that serves the program or the staff who run it.","note":"Why it lands: the governance-versus-operations line is the most useful distinction any board member can wield. Asking it as a genuine question, not a rebuke, keeps the board out of the weeds while marking you as someone who understands the role. Note you fold your own interest in by mentioning the staff."},{"id":"fl-int-12","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'm going to push back, | and I want to be clear it's on the substance, not on anyone in the room. | My concern is *materiality* – | we're about to spend a third of the meeting on an exposure that, if I've understood it, is genuinely small. | I'd rather we protected our time for the decision that actually carries risk.","note":"Why it lands: announcing the push-back before making it reads as confident. Separating substance from person protects the relationship. 'Materiality' triages what deserves board attention – a sophisticated way to say 'this isn't worth our time' without dismissing the person who raised it."},{"id":"fl-int-13","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"On the spot","say":"I should *declare a conflict* on this one. | Given my role in the program, it's not appropriate for me to weigh in on the decision, | so I'll make my reasoning available if it's useful and then step back from the vote.","note":"Why it lands: declaring a conflict proactively is the strongest integrity move on a board, and it directly fits your overlapping roles. Far from weakening you, it builds the standing you'll draw on when you do hold firm on a genuine governance matter later. Have this one ready."},{"id":"fl-int-14","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Close","say":"Where I'd *land* is in-principle support, | contingent on us seeing the budget before anything's committed. | That lets the work move forward without the board signing a blank cheque. | I'd be comfortable putting that as a motion.","note":"Why it lands: 'in-principle support, contingent on' is the precise instrument that lets a board say a constructive yes without losing control. Offering to put it as a motion is quietly decisive – you're not just commenting, you're moving the room to a decision."},{"id":"fl-int-15","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Build","say":"I'd endorse what Kevin said, | and I'd add the one thing that, for me, settles it. | This is in *mission alignment* – | it serves the reason the program exists in the first place, | and on a board that's the test that should outrank the logistics.","note":"Why it lands: agreeing then adding 'the one thing that settles it' positions you as the person who brings the decisive frame. Lifting the discussion to mission is the board's proper altitude. You look intelligent here not by sounding clever but by raising the conversation to where it should sit."},{"id":"fl-int-16","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Open","say":"I'd like to put a *stake in the ground* early, so the discussion has something to react to. | My view is that we proceed, with a review clause at the end of the first year. | I'm open to being moved off that, | but I think it's more useful than starting from a blank page.","note":"Why it lands: volunteering a clear position to anchor the room is a leadership act, especially early when others are hedging. 'I'm open to being moved off that' keeps it from reading as rigid. Diction note: 'stake in the ground' needs crisp stops on the hard consonants or it muddies."},{"id":"fl-int-17","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Challenge","say":"Help me *understand* the reasoning. | We're proposing to lead with the budget, | but if the academic case isn't settled, the budget is answering a question we haven't asked yet. | What am I missing?","note":"Why it lands: challenging by asking is the most senior move in any academic room – it's impossible to be defensive against a genuine question. 'What am I missing' is generous and confident at once. Said level, with no edge, it dismantles a weak proposal more effectively than any assertion."},{"id":"fl-int-18","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"On the spot","say":"I want to give you a straight answer, | so let me think for a second rather than fill the silence. | *pause* | Right – my honest read is that we're not ready, and I'd rather defer than commit to a date we'll miss.","note":"Why it lands: narrating the pause ('let me think rather than fill the silence') gives you permission to stop talking, which is the cure for the stumble. The silence itself reads as composure. Practise actually holding the [pause] – count two full seconds. This is the most important diction drill in the set: saying nothing, clearly."},{"id":"fl-int-19","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Close","say":"I think we're *closer* than the discussion suggests. | The disagreement is about sequencing, not direction. | If we can agree to take staffing first and revisit the timeline in a fortnight, | I suspect we're all in the same place.","note":"Why it lands: reframing a heated discussion as 'closer than it sounds' is a calming, authoritative move that lets everyone climb down without losing face. Naming the disagreement precisely (sequencing, not direction) shows you were actually listening, which is its own form of command."},{"id":"fl-int-20","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Open","say":"I'd frame our task narrowly, if I may. | We're not being asked to redesign the course – | we're being asked whether this revision preserves *comparability* across school contexts. | That's the question I'd keep us anchored to.","note":"Why it lands: narrowing the committee's task is a quietly powerful chairing move even when you're not the chair. 'Comparability across school contexts' is the precise SCSA concern. Diction note: 'comparability' is a five-syllable trap – break it com-pa-ra-bil-i-ty, don't let the middle collapse."},{"id":"fl-int-21","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'd want to slow this down. | There's an *implementation* risk we're stepping past – | schools in smaller centres won't have the staff to deliver this in the timeframe, | and our advice has to account for them, not just the well-resourced schools.","note":"Why it lands: 'slow this down' is a deliberate act of control over a rushing room. Raising equity for under-resourced schools aligns you with SCSA's stated values, so the challenge is principled rather than obstructive. 'Implementation' is a four-syllable word people slur – land each beat."},{"id":"fl-int-22","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Close","say":"Can I offer a *synthesis*. | We support the intent, | we have a genuine concern about timeline and equity of access, | and we'd advise phased rollout with proper lead time for professional learning. | Does that capture the room?","note":"Why it lands: 'offer a synthesis' is the elevated, accurate word for pulling threads together, and it fits a standards body. Ending with 'does that capture the room' invites correction and makes the summary collective rather than imposed. Diction note: 'synthesis' and 'phased' both need clean fricatives."},{"id":"fl-int-23","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Build","say":"I'd reinforce Penelope's point and put it more strongly. | Consensus advice that papers over a real *equity* concern isn't consensus – it's avoidance. | I'd rather we named the difficulty plainly and advised accordingly.","note":"Why it lands: agreeing and then strengthening ('put it more strongly') is intelligent agreement at its best – you add courage to someone else's point. Distinguishing genuine consensus from avoidance is a sharp, quotable distinction that marks you as a serious thinker in the room."},{"id":"fl-int-24","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Open","say":"Before the detail, one *governance* question. | Are we the right body to be deciding this, | or are we about to make an operational call that belongs with the executive? | I'd want that settled before we spend time on the substance.","note":"Why it lands: opening on the governance-operations boundary is the board member's sharpest instrument. Asking rather than asserting keeps it collegial. Diction note: 'governance' and 'operational' are both multisyllabic – slow down through them or they blur into mush under nerves."},{"id":"fl-int-25","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'm going to register a *respectful* dissent. | I understand where the majority sits, and I won't hold the meeting up, | but I'd want it minuted that I raised the resourcing risk | so the record is honest about it.","note":"Why it lands: 'respectful dissent' lets you hold a minority position with total composure. Saying you won't hold things up shows you understand collective responsibility; asking for it to be minuted protects you without seeming combative. This is how a senior board member disagrees and loses gracefully while keeping their integrity intact."},{"id":"fl-int-26","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"On the spot","say":"That's not something I can *responsibly* answer off the cuff, | and I don't think you'd want me to. | Let me get the figures and come back to the board with something accurate | rather than something fast.","note":"Why it lands: 'I don't think you'd want me to' reframes your non-answer as serving the board, not protecting yourself. The accurate-versus-fast contrast is a clean, repeatable structure. 'Responsibly' is a five-syllable word – re-spon-si-bly – and slurring it undercuts the very composure you're projecting."},{"id":"fl-int-27","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Close","say":"Let me draw this to a *close*. | We have in-principle agreement, | one dissent that's properly minuted, | and an action on the executive to bring the budget back next meeting. | I'd take a motion to that effect.","note":"Why it lands: 'draw this to a close' is a clean chairing phrase that signals the discussion is done. Acknowledging the dissent in the summary is gracious and honest. Moving straight to a motion is decisive – you're converting talk into a decision, which is the whole point of a board."},{"id":"fl-int-28","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Build","say":"I want to support that, | and name why it matters beyond this one decision. | If we get the *stewardship* principle right here, | it sets the precedent for every resourcing call we make after it. | That's why I think it's worth getting exactly right.","note":"Why it lands: agreeing and then widening the frame ('beyond this one decision') shows strategic range – you see the precedent, not just the instance. 'Stewardship' is warm and weighty, ideal for a values-driven board. It earns respect by demonstrating you think in years, not items."},{"id":"fl-int-29","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Open","say":"I'll be brief, because I think the issue is *narrower* than the paper suggests. | Most of what's written here we agree on. | The live question is one line on page three, | and I'd suggest we spend our time there rather than relitigating the rest.","note":"Why it lands: narrowing a sprawling paper to its single live question is a chairing instinct that reads as command even from a member. Saying you'll be brief and then being brief builds trust the room will extend to you next time."},{"id":"fl-int-30","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'd want to separate correlation from *causation* here. | Attainment and attendance move together in the data, | but term length might be driving both, | and if it is, the intervention we're proposing won't touch the actual cause.","note":"Why it lands: naming a confound is rigorous and specific, not vague scepticism. You're not saying 'I disagree', you're naming the precise mechanism by which the argument might fail. 'Causation' must be landed cleanly – cau-sa-tion – to carry the weight."},{"id":"fl-int-31","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"On the spot","say":"I can give you a partial answer now and a *complete* one next week. | What I know is the principle; what I'd need to confirm is the cost. | I'd rather flag that boundary clearly than blur it.","note":"Why it lands: separating what you know from what you'd need to confirm is the single most credible thing you can do when caught out. It converts 'I don't fully know' into a precise, confident map of the gap. Flagging the boundary rather than blurring it is exactly the composure that stops a stumble."},{"id":"fl-int-32","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Close","say":"Let me name where I think we've *converged*. | The principle is agreed. | The two open items are timeline and resourcing, | and I'd propose the working group brings both back with options rather than a single recommendation. | Comfortable with that?","note":"Why it lands: 'converged' is precise and quietly elevated. Asking for options rather than a single recommendation respects the committee's role in deciding, which marks you as someone who understands governance. 'Comfortable with that' hands the close back to the room."},{"id":"fl-int-33","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"Build","say":"I'd reinforce that, | and draw out the implication people might be missing. | If we accept the *premise*, | then the resourcing question answers itself – we've already committed to it in principle. | So the real decision was made earlier than we think.","note":"Why it lands: following an argument to its logical implication, and showing the room they've already half-decided, is a sophisticated build. You're not adding volume, you're adding insight. That's the kind of contribution that gets you listened to before you've finished speaking."},{"id":"fl-int-34","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Open","say":"I'd anchor us to one principle before we start. | Whatever we advise has to hold up on *equity of access*, | because that's the test these decisions are ultimately judged against. | If a proposal fails that test, the rest doesn't matter much.","note":"Why it lands: opening by setting the test the discussion will be measured against quietly shapes the entire conversation in your favour. 'Equity of access' is a value SCSA is bound to. You've framed the criteria, which is more powerful than arguing within someone else's."},{"id":"fl-int-35","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Challenge","say":"I think we're at risk of advising on *content* when the real issue is *assessment*. | The syllabus reads fine. | What I can't see is how a teacher in a small school moderates this fairly, | and that's the question that actually determines whether it works.","note":"Why it lands: redirecting from content to assessment shows deep familiarity with where curriculum decisions actually succeed or fail. Naming the small-school teacher grounds an abstract concern in a real person, which is persuasive in a way that principle alone isn't."},{"id":"fl-int-36","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"On the spot","say":"I'd want to be careful not to answer that too *quickly*. | There's a moderation dimension I haven't fully thought through, | and I'd rather bring considered advice than a fast opinion that doesn't hold. | Can I come back to it?","note":"Why it lands: 'careful not to answer too quickly' makes deliberation visible and admirable. In a standards body, considered beats fast every time, and saying so explicitly aligns you with the body's own values. A clean, reusable way to buy thinking time."},{"id":"fl-int-37","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Close","say":"If I can pull the threads together. | We support the intent, | our advice is conditional on a workable *implementation* timeline, | and we want the moderation guidance strengthened before rollout. | I think that's a position we can all sign.","note":"Why it lands: 'a position we can all sign' invokes the consensus model directly – you're doing the committee's actual job, which is producing advice everyone can stand behind. Listing the conditions cleanly shows you've tracked the whole discussion."},{"id":"fl-int-38","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"Build","say":"I'd back that and sharpen one word. | This isn't a *refinement* of the existing standard – it's a genuine raising of it, | and if that's what we're doing, we should say so plainly so schools can prepare. | Naming it honestly is part of our duty.","note":"Why it lands: insisting on the honest word ('not a refinement, a raising') is intellectual integrity made visible. You're agreeing while improving the precision, and tying it to the committee's duty to schools. That combination – agreeable and exacting – is exactly the respect-commanding move you asked about."},{"id":"fl-int-39","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Open","say":"I'd like to frame the decision before we discuss it. | This is fundamentally a question of *risk appetite* – | are we a board that trials and reviews, or one that waits for certainty? | If we settle that, the specific call becomes much easier.","note":"Why it lands: reframing a yes/no decision as a question about the board's own character is a senior move that lifts the discussion above the immediate item. 'Risk appetite' is precise governance language. You've made the abstract decision concrete and the concrete one easy."},{"id":"fl-int-40","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Challenge","say":"I'd gently challenge the framing. | We're treating this as a financial decision, | but the *material* risk here isn't financial – it's reputational, | and that's a different calculation with different people who need to be consulted.","note":"Why it lands: 'gently challenge the framing' disagrees with the structure of the discussion, not a person, which is the least defensive way to redirect a board. Distinguishing reputational from financial risk shows range. 'Material' is the precise word for 'significant enough to act on'."},{"id":"fl-int-41","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"On the spot","say":"I don't want to give the board a number I'm not *confident* in. | Let me confirm it and circulate it before we meet, | so the decision rests on something solid rather than my memory under pressure.","note":"Why it lands: admitting you won't trust your memory under pressure is disarmingly honest and reads as exactly the diligence a board wants. Offering to circulate beforehand keeps the process moving. This is the on-the-spot move that protects you from the stumble entirely – you decline to perform certainty you don't have."},{"id":"fl-int-42","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Close","say":"I'll summarise so the minutes are *clean*. | In-principle support, | subject to the budget returning next meeting, | with my reputational concern noted. | If that's right, I'd move it formally.","note":"Why it lands: 'so the minutes are clean' shows you're thinking about the record, which is a governance instinct. A tight, structured summary delivered calmly is one of the most authoritative things a board member can do. Offering to move it converts your summary into momentum."},{"id":"fl-int-43","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Build","say":"I strongly support that, | and I'd add the long view. | Decisions like this are where a board either builds or spends its *credibility*, | and I think this one builds it – | which is reason enough to do it properly rather than quickly.","note":"Why it lands: framing the decision as an investment in the board's own credibility is a mature, strategic build. You're agreeing and simultaneously raising the stakes in a constructive direction. 'Builds or spends its credibility' is a quotable formulation that people remember."},{"id":"fl-int-44","family":"Interventions","room":"University","fn":"On the spot","say":"Can I have a moment to give you a *considered* answer. | *pause* | My instinct says yes, | but my instinct isn't what the committee needs – it needs the reasoning, | and I'd like to get that right before I commit us.","note":"Why it lands: asking for a moment out loud, then taking it, is the most direct training for the stumble there is. Distinguishing your instinct from the reasoning the committee needs is humble and rigorous at once. Hold the [pause] for real – that silence is the whole exercise."},{"id":"fl-int-45","family":"Interventions","room":"SCSA","fn":"On the spot","say":"That deserves a *precise* answer, not an approximate one. | Let me check the moderation data and respond properly, | because a wrong figure here would propagate into advice that affects every school.","note":"Why it lands: 'deserves a precise answer' flatters the question while declining to wing it. Naming the downstream consequence – advice affecting every school – justifies the care without sounding evasive. A clean way to refuse to be rushed in a standards context."},{"id":"fl-int-46","family":"Interventions","room":"Board","fn":"Challenge","say":"I want to register one *reservation* without blocking anything. | I think we're under-weighting the staffing risk. | I'll support the motion, | but I'd like my concern on the record so we revisit it if the risk materialises.","note":"Why it lands: supporting while registering a reservation is the sophisticated board move – you're not obstructive, but you've protected the future conversation. 'If the risk materialises' plants a flag that makes you look prescient later if it does. Composed disagreement that costs you nothing."}],"pairs":[{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-1","family":"Meetings","weak":"I just wanted to maybe suggest that perhaps we could look at...","strong":"I'm proposing we do this. Here's why.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-2","family":"Meetings","weak":"Sorry, does that make sense? Sorry to go on...","strong":"I'll pause there. Questions?","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-3","family":"Meetings","weak":"I think it might possibly be a bit of an issue that...","strong":"There's a problem we need to name.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-4","family":"Meetings","weak":"Yeah, no, totally, but like, the thing is...","strong":"I see it differently. Here's where.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-5","family":"Meetings","weak":"I don't know, what does everyone else think?","strong":"My recommendation is X. I want to hear objections before we lock it.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-6","family":"Meetings","weak":"I was just thinking, and tell me if I'm wrong, but...","strong":"Here's my read on it.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-7","family":"Meetings","weak":"Could we maybe possibly think about pushing the date, if that's okay?","strong":"I want to move the date. Here's the reason.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-8","family":"Meetings","weak":"I'm probably overthinking this but...","strong":"One concern, and it's a real one.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-9","family":"Meetings","weak":"Sorry to jump in, I'll be quick, I promise...","strong":"Before we move on, one point.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-10","family":"Meetings","weak":"I guess we could go either way really, I don't mind...","strong":"I'd go with the first option. Here's why it's the stronger one.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-11","family":"Meetings","weak":"I mean, it's just my opinion, but...","strong":"My view is clear on this.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-meeting-12","family":"Meetings","weak":"Does anyone have any thoughts at all on, um, any of this?","strong":"I want two things from this discussion. Let's start with the first.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-1","family":"Parents","weak":"I'm so sorry to have to email you about this, I hope it's okay...","strong":"I'm writing to let you know where things stand with [student].","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-2","family":"Parents","weak":"We were sort of hoping that maybe [student] could perhaps try to...","strong":"For [student] to continue in the ensemble, we need [specific thing] by [date].","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-3","family":"Parents","weak":"It's totally fine if not but it would be really great if...","strong":"Please confirm attendance by Friday so we can finalise the program.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-4","family":"Parents","weak":"I completely understand and I'm happy to do whatever works for you...","strong":"I understand. Here's what I can offer, and here's what I can't.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-5","family":"Parents","weak":"I don't want to be a bother but I noticed [student] has missed a few...","strong":"[Student] has missed three rehearsals. I want to sort out why and how we fix it.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-6","family":"Parents","weak":"Sorry, I know you're busy, just following up again on the form...","strong":"I still need the form to enrol [student]. Can you return it by Wednesday?","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-7","family":"Parents","weak":"We'd really love it if you could possibly consider maybe coming along...","strong":"The showcase is on [date]. I'd encourage you to be there for [student].","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-8","family":"Parents","weak":"I hope I'm not overstepping but I think there might be a small concern...","strong":"I want to raise something about [student]'s progress directly with you.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-9","family":"Parents","weak":"Whatever you decide is completely fine, no pressure at all, honestly...","strong":"Take the week to decide. I'll need your answer by Friday either way.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-parent-10","family":"Parents","weak":"I'm really sorry, I know this is short notice and probably annoying...","strong":"This is short notice, and I'm sorry for that. Here's what's changed and what it means.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-1","family":"Council","weak":"Um, I guess we should probably move to the next item if that's okay with everyone?","strong":"Moving to item four. [Name], over to you.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-2","family":"Council","weak":"I don't really mind either way, whatever the group thinks is best...","strong":"As Chair, my view is X. I'll take a motion.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-3","family":"Council","weak":"Sorry, I know we're short on time, but could I just quickly...","strong":"One point before we close, then we're done.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-4","family":"Council","weak":"I think we kind of need to maybe revisit this at some point...","strong":"We'll revisit this on [date]. I'm noting it as an action.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-5","family":"Council","weak":"Does anyone want to maybe say anything before we, um, wrap up?","strong":"Final comments. Then I'm closing the meeting.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-6","family":"Council","weak":"I suppose we could vote on it if people wanted to, no pressure...","strong":"I'm putting this to a vote. All in favour?","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-7","family":"Council","weak":"Sorry, I'm not sure we're really staying on topic here...","strong":"We're off the agenda. Let's come back to item three.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-8","family":"Council","weak":"I think maybe we've sort of run a bit over, should we...","strong":"We're at time. I'll carry the rest to next meeting.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-9","family":"Council","weak":"It would be great if someone could possibly take that on, if anyone's free...","strong":"[Name], can you own this action? I'll record it against you.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-council-10","family":"Council","weak":"I just want to make sure everyone's happy before we decide anything...","strong":"I've heard the room. Here's the decision I'm putting forward.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-1","family":"Boundaries","weak":"I mean, I could probably try to fit it in somehow, I guess...","strong":"I can't take that on right now. My plate's full through August.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-2","family":"Boundaries","weak":"It's fine, don't worry, I'll just sort it out myself...","strong":"That's yours to handle. Tell me if you get stuck.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-3","family":"Boundaries","weak":"I really don't want to make a fuss but it's been bothering me a little...","strong":"I need to raise something directly with you.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-4","family":"Boundaries","weak":"Maybe I'm overreacting but it kind of felt like...","strong":"When X happened, the effect was Y. I want it handled differently.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-5","family":"Boundaries","weak":"I suppose I can stay late again if it's really needed...","strong":"I'm not available after four. Let's find another way.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-6","family":"Boundaries","weak":"Sorry, it's probably my fault for not being clearer earlier...","strong":"Let me be clear now, so there's no confusion going forward.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-7","family":"Boundaries","weak":"I don't want to step on anyone's toes but I think that's my area...","strong":"That's my call to make. I'd like to be consulted before it's decided.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-8","family":"Boundaries","weak":"I guess I can keep doing it for now if no one else can...","strong":"This needs to move to someone else. I've carried it long enough.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-9","family":"Boundaries","weak":"It's okay, really, I don't want to cause any drama about it...","strong":"This matters to me, and I want it addressed properly.","note":""},{"id":"fl-pair-boundary-10","family":"Boundaries","weak":"Maybe we could possibly talk about how that was handled, if you have time?","strong":"I want ten minutes to talk about how that was handled.","note":""}],"words":[{"id":"fl-vic-committee-1","register":"Committee moves","word":"Can I offer a different read on that","sense":"entering a contested point without combat","say":"*Can I offer a different read on that* – I think the cause sits one step earlier.","note":"Backfires when: followed by agreement. If you announce a different read, deliver one."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-2","register":"Committee moves","word":"I want to test that a little","sense":"challenging a claim without attacking the person","say":"*I want to test that a little*: what happens to the model if enrolments fall?","note":"Backfires when: used as a soft wrapper for 'you're wrong'. It works because it's genuinely curious."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-3","register":"Committee moves","word":"Let me build on what [name] said","sense":"taking the floor by crediting, not interrupting","say":"*Let me build on what Kevin said* – the staffing point extends to the camp too.","note":"Backfires when: you don't actually build, you redirect. The room notices the bait-and-switch."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-4","register":"Committee moves","word":"I'd want to separate two things here","sense":"slowing a muddled discussion with authority","say":"*I'd want to separate two things here*: the principle, and the timing.","note":"Backfires when: there aren't actually two things. Don't manufacture structure to sound rigorous."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-5","register":"Committee moves","word":"Where I'd land is","sense":"stating a position as settled, not tentative","say":"*Where I'd land is* that we trial it for one term and review against numbers.","note":"Backfires when: said early. It's a closing move – earn it by hearing the room first."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-6","register":"Committee moves","word":"I'm comfortable being the dissenting voice on this","sense":"holding a minority position with composure","say":"*I'm comfortable being the dissenting voice on this*, and I'll say why briefly.","note":"Backfires when: used to be contrarian. Reserve it for when you genuinely hold the line alone."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-7","register":"Committee moves","word":"Can we be clear on what we're actually deciding","sense":"forcing a drifting committee to a decision","say":"*Can we be clear on what we're actually deciding* before we go further?","note":"Backfires when: the answer is obvious to everyone but you. Use it when the room has genuinely drifted."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-8","register":"Committee moves","word":"I'll defer to [name] on the detail, but on principle","sense":"conceding ground while holding your position","say":"*I'll defer to David on the detail, but on principle* I think the direction is wrong.","note":"Backfires when: you defer on the thing that actually matters. Concede the small, hold the large."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-9","register":"Committee moves","word":"That's the right question, and I don't think we have the answer yet","sense":"validating without faking certainty","say":"*That's the right question, and I don't think we have the answer yet* – which is itself worth noting.","note":"Backfires when: used to dodge. It's powerful only because it's honest about a real gap."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-10","register":"Committee moves","word":"Let me put a stake in the ground","sense":"committing to a position to move the room","say":"*Let me put a stake in the ground*: I think we proceed, and I'll own the risk.","note":"Backfires when: overused. A committee that hears it every meeting stops feeling the weight of it."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-11","register":"Committee moves","word":"I think we're solving the wrong problem","sense":"reframing the entire discussion","say":"*I think we're solving the wrong problem* – the issue isn't cost, it's capacity.","note":"Backfires when: you can't immediately name the right one. Only deploy it with the reframe ready."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-12","register":"Committee moves","word":"I'll be the one to say it","sense":"naming what the room is avoiding","say":"*I'll be the one to say it*: this timeline was never realistic.","note":"Backfires when: what follows is mild. The phrase promises candour – pay it off."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-13","register":"Committee moves","word":"Help me understand the reasoning","sense":"challenging by asking, the most senior move there is","say":"*Help me understand the reasoning* behind starting with the budget rather than the staffing.","note":"Backfires when: said with an edge. It only reads as senior when it's genuinely level."},{"id":"fl-vic-committee-14","register":"Committee moves","word":"I'd rather we got this right than quick","sense":"resisting pressure to rush, calmly","say":"*I'd rather we got this right than quick*, even if it means carrying it to next meeting.","note":"Backfires when: used to stall something you simply don't want. The room can tell the difference."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-1","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Steel-man before you dissent","sense":"state the opposing case at its strongest, then disagree","say":"*The strongest version of your argument is X, and I still don't accept it – here's the one place it breaks.*","note":"Backfires when: the steel-man is a straw-man in disguise. If you misrepresent the case to look fair, a sharp room catches it instantly and you lose the standing the move was meant to buy."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-2","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Concede to gain","sense":"grant the strong point so your real objection lands clean","say":"*You're right about the cost, completely. That's not where my objection sits.*","note":"Backfires when: you concede the thing that actually mattered. Give away the peripheral, never the load-bearing point."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-3","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Name the meta","sense":"step up a level and describe the conversation itself","say":"*I think we're having two conversations at once – one about principle, one about logistics – and they're tangling.*","note":"Backfires when: there's only one conversation and you've invented a second to sound perceptive."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-4","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"The reframing question","sense":"a question that resets the terms without confrontation","say":"*What would we have to believe for this to be the right call?*","note":"Backfires when: used to lead a witness. It works because it's open – the moment it's rhetorical, it reads as a trap."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-5","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Grant the premise, deny the conclusion","sense":"accept the facts, reject what's drawn from them","say":"*I'll grant every figure on that slide. I don't accept that they point where you say they do.*","note":"Backfires when: you can't articulate the gap between premise and conclusion. If you grant the premise you must show precisely where the inference fails."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-6","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"The deliberate concession of uncertainty","sense":"naming the limit of your own knowledge as a position of strength","say":"*I can take this to the edge of what I know, and then I'll tell you we're guessing.*","note":"Backfires when: overused – a person who is uncertain about everything commands nothing. It lands because it's rare and precise."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-7","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Isolate the crux","sense":"strip a sprawling disagreement to the single decisive question","say":"*Set everything else aside. This entire decision turns on one question: can we staff it sustainably?*","note":"Backfires when: you isolate the wrong crux. Get it right and the room follows you; get it wrong and you've narrowed to a side issue."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-8","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"The principled exception","sense":"hold the rule while granting this one case","say":"*I'm against making this routine. For these specific circumstances, once, I'd support it.*","note":"Backfires when: the 'exception' is really a reversal. If you do it every time, you didn't hold a principle."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-9","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Defer the decision, not the thinking","sense":"refuse to rush a call without looking passive","say":"*I don't want a decision today. I do want us to leave knowing exactly what we're deciding next time.*","note":"Backfires when: it's avoidance dressed as rigour. Pair it with a concrete next step or it reads as a stall."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-10","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Acknowledge the cost of your own position","sense":"pre-empt the counter by naming what your view sacrifices","say":"*My recommendation has a real cost – it slows us a term. I think that cost is worth paying, and here's why.*","note":"Backfires when: the named cost is trivial. Naming a fake weakness to seem balanced is transparent."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-11","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"The summarising close","sense":"take the floor at the end by stating where the room landed","say":"*Let me say back what I think we've agreed, so we're not relitigating it next month.*","note":"Backfires when: your summary smuggles in your preference. Summarise honestly or the room stops trusting the move."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-12","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Separate the person from the position","sense":"disagree hard while leaving the relationship intact","say":"*I have a lot of respect for how you've run this, and I think this particular call is wrong.*","note":"Backfires when: the warm clause is perfunctory. It only works if the respect is real and evident."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-13","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"The cost-of-delay frame","sense":"reframe inaction as itself a decision with consequences","say":"*Waiting isn't the neutral option here – every term we wait, the cohort gets harder to recover.*","note":"Backfires when: the cost is speculative. Use it when delay genuinely compounds, not as a pressure tactic."},{"id":"fl-vic-rhetorical-14","register":"Rhetorical moves","word":"Yield the floor deliberately","sense":"hand off in a way that keeps your authority","say":"*I've said my piece. I'd genuinely like to hear the case against it before we move.*","note":"Backfires when: you don't mean it and interrupt the answer. Yielding only reads as strong if you actually listen."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-1","register":"High register","word":"Orthogonal","sense":"unrelated; on a different axis entirely","say":"That's an important issue, but it's *orthogonal* to what we're deciding.","note":"Register: safe in research and policy committees, where the mathematical sense is understood. In a mixed board or parent-facing room it reads as showing off – say 'a separate question' instead."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-2","register":"High register","word":"Isomorphic","sense":"structurally identical though different in surface","say":"The staffing problem is *isomorphic* to the one we solved for the strings program.","note":"Register: only among people who'll recognise it – a technical or academic committee. Anywhere else it's friction, not signal. 'Structurally the same' carries it."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-3","register":"High register","word":"A priori","sense":"reasoned from principle, before the evidence","say":"There's no *a priori* reason it has to run in Term 2 rather than Term 3.","note":"Register: at home in scholarly rooms. Don't use it where it'll sound like Latin for its own sake – and never mispair it with 'a posteriori' just to complete the set."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-4","register":"High register","word":"Ipso facto","sense":"by that very fact","say":"If the ensemble can't field a section, it *ipso facto* can't perform the program.","note":"Register: high-risk. In the right room it's crisp; in most it sounds theatrical. 'By definition' does the same work with no cost."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-5","register":"High register","word":"Sine qua non","sense":"an absolutely indispensable condition","say":"Reliable relief staffing is the *sine qua non* of running four ensembles.","note":"Register: reserve for genuinely scholarly company and use it once. Twice in a meeting and it tips into performance."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-6","register":"High register","word":"Tendentious","sense":"slanted to push a particular conclusion","say":"I'd call that framing *tendentious* – it's built to lead us somewhere.","note":"Register: sharp and useful in an argument among peers who'll hear it as precise rather than as an insult. It does carry an edge – deploy it knowingly."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-7","register":"High register","word":"Specious","sense":"superficially convincing but actually flawed","say":"The cost argument is *specious* – it looks decisive until you account for retention.","note":"Register: safe in most professional rooms and genuinely precise. Just be sure you can show the flaw, since the word promises you've found one."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-8","register":"High register","word":"Prima facie","sense":"on first appearance, before deeper scrutiny","say":"*Prima facie* it looks like a budget problem, but I think it's a scheduling one.","note":"Register: widely understood and low-risk in senior professional settings. One of the safer Latinate options."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-9","register":"High register","word":"Necessary but not sufficient","sense":"required, yet not enough on its own","say":"Funding is *necessary but not sufficient* – without the staff it changes nothing.","note":"Register: universally safe and quietly impressive. This is the high-register move that almost never backfires."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-10","register":"High register","word":"Begs the question","sense":"assumes the very thing in dispute (true sense)","say":"That *begs the question* – it assumes the program's the problem, which is what we're testing.","note":"Register: risky precisely because half the room uses it to mean 'raises the question'. Among logicians and philosophers the strict sense lands; elsewhere you'll be misheard. Know your audience."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-11","register":"High register","word":"Asymmetry","sense":"an imbalance between two sides","say":"There's an *asymmetry* here: we carry all the risk, they take the credit.","note":"Register: broadly safe and genuinely useful for naming an unfairness without saying 'unfair'. Low risk."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-12","register":"High register","word":"Categorical","sense":"absolute, admitting no exception","say":"My objection is *categorical*, not a matter of degree.","note":"Register: safe and forceful. The only risk is using it for something that is in fact a matter of degree – then it's just overstatement."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-13","register":"High register","word":"Confound (a variable)","sense":"a hidden factor distorting an apparent link","say":"Attendance and attainment track together, but term length might be *confounding* both.","note":"Register: at home in any evidence-literate room and a genuine mark of rigour. Misfires only if used where there's no actual data relationship to confound."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-14","register":"High register","word":"Load-bearing","sense":"the assumption everything else rests on","say":"That one figure is doing all the *load-bearing* work in the whole proposal.","note":"Register: increasingly current in sharp professional rooms, plainer than its Latinate cousins, and vivid. Among the safest 'impressive' options because it's concrete."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-15","register":"High register","word":"Mutatis mutandis","sense":"with the necessary changes made","say":"The same logic applies to the strings program, *mutatis mutandis*.","note":"Register: very high-risk – only among lawyers, philosophers, or senior academics who'll recognise it. Anywhere else it's pure affectation. 'With the obvious adjustments' is almost always better."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-16","register":"High register","word":"Pari passu","sense":"on an equal footing, proceeding together","say":"I'd want both programs funded *pari passu*, not one ahead of the other.","note":"Register: finance and law boards know it; a school staffroom will not. Confined to its native rooms it's crisp, elsewhere it alienates."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-17","register":"High register","word":"Inter alia","sense":"among other things","say":"The review covers staffing and timetabling, *inter alia*.","note":"Register: common in formal governance writing, riskier aloud. In a scholarly committee it passes; in a parent-facing room say 'among other things'."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-18","register":"High register","word":"De minimis","sense":"too small to warrant attention","say":"The cost difference is *de minimis* – not worth the meeting time.","note":"Register: safe in finance, audit, and legal-literate boards. 'Negligible' carries it everywhere with no risk."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-19","register":"High register","word":"Bona fide","sense":"genuine, in good faith","say":"It's a *bona fide* concern, not a procedural objection.","note":"Register: widely understood and low-risk; one of the safer Latin phrases. Just don't mispronounce it."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-20","register":"High register","word":"Ceteris paribus","sense":"all else being equal","say":"*Ceteris paribus*, the larger cohort should perform better – but all else is rarely equal.","note":"Register: economists and academics use it freely; elsewhere it's showing off. The English version costs you nothing."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-21","register":"High register","word":"Ex ante / ex post","sense":"before the event / after the event","say":"This looked reasonable *ex ante*; *ex post* we can see the flaw.","note":"Register: precise and respected in policy and economics rooms. Pair them as a contrast or not at all."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-22","register":"High register","word":"Dialectic","sense":"truth reached through opposing arguments","say":"I'd rather we treated this as a *dialectic* than a vote – the disagreement is doing useful work.","note":"Register: at home among philosophers and serious academics. In a board it can read as grandiose; gauge the room."},{"id":"fl-vic-highregister-23","register":"High register","word":"Heuristic","sense":"a rule of thumb, not a guarantee","say":"That's a useful *heuristic*, but I wouldn't build policy on it.","note":"Register: broadly understood in educated rooms and genuinely useful. Low risk; just don't use it where 'rule of thumb' is warmer."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-1","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Pedagogy","sense":"the method and practice of teaching","say":"Our *pedagogy* has to lead the timetable, not the other way around.","note":"Backfires when: used to dress up a point that 'teaching' would have said more plainly."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-2","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Differentiate","sense":"tailor teaching to varied student needs","say":"We *differentiate* the parts so the weaker readers aren't left behind.","note":"Backfires when: used as jargon without an actual example of how."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-3","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Scaffold","sense":"build support that's gradually removed","say":"I'd *scaffold* the harmony over three lessons rather than front-load it.","note":"Backfires when: stretched to mean 'help' generally. Keep it to staged support."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-4","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Formative","sense":"assessment that guides learning, not grades it","say":"Treat the first run-through as *formative* – it tells us where to spend rehearsal time.","note":"Backfires when: paired with 'summative' in the same breath just to sound technical."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-5","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Cohort","sense":"a group moving through together","say":"This *cohort* is stronger on rhythm than last year's, weaker on sight-reading.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'class' or 'year group' is the natural word."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-6","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Efficacy","sense":"whether something actually works","say":"I want evidence of *efficacy* before we roll this across every ensemble.","note":"Backfires when: swapped in for 'effectiveness' purely for weight. Reserve it for genuine evaluation."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-7","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Pitch (it)","sense":"set the level of difficulty","say":"We've *pitched* this too high for a first-year group.","note":"Backfires when: never – this is a plain, precise teaching word. Use it freely."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-8","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Trajectory","sense":"the path of development over time","say":"Her *trajectory* over two terms matters more than any single performance.","note":"Backfires when: applied to a single moment. It only means something across time."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-9","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Threshold","sense":"the point at which something changes in kind","say":"There's a *threshold* below which an ensemble simply can't function – we're near it.","note":"Backfires when: used for any old limit. Reserve it for a genuine tipping point."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-10","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Calibrate","sense":"adjust precisely against a standard","say":"We need to *calibrate* the expectations to what a Year 8 cohort can actually carry.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'adjust' or 'set' is plainer. Keep it for fine-tuning against a benchmark."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-11","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Mastery","sense":"deep, secure command of a skill","say":"I'd rather they reached *mastery* on three pieces than skated across ten.","note":"Backfires when: overclaimed. It's a high bar – don't use it for 'pretty good'."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-12","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Antecedent","sense":"what came before and shaped this","say":"The *antecedent* issue is primary-school provision, not anything we're doing here.","note":"Backfires when: 'cause' or 'root' would land harder. Use it when sequence genuinely matters."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-13","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Provision","sense":"what is formally supplied or made available","say":"The *provision* for instrumental tuition hasn't kept pace with enrolment.","note":"Backfires when: used vaguely. It carries weight precisely because it implies a formal entitlement."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-14","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Coherent","sense":"holding together as a unified whole","say":"I want a *coherent* pathway from Year 7 to Year 12, not a set of disconnected years.","note":"Backfires when: used as filler praise. It means parts that genuinely fit – show the fit."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-15","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Constructivist","sense":"learning built actively by the student, not transmitted","say":"A *constructivist* approach would have them discover the harmony before we name it.","note":"Backfires when: dropped as a label without the practice behind it. Pedagogues will test whether you mean it."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-16","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Metacognition","sense":"students thinking about their own thinking","say":"The real gain is *metacognition* – they start to hear their own mistakes before I do.","note":"Backfires when: used to sound current. Reserve it for genuine self-monitoring, not any reflection."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-17","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Benchmark","sense":"a reference standard to measure against","say":"Let's *benchmark* against the state ensembles, not against last year's cohort alone.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'compare' is plainer. Keep it for measurement against a defined standard."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-18","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Attainment","sense":"the level a student actually reaches","say":"Participation is high; *attainment* is where I want to see movement.","note":"Backfires when: conflated with effort or engagement. It specifically means measured achievement."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-19","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Authentic assessment","sense":"testing through real-world tasks, not proxies","say":"A performance is *authentic assessment* – it tests the thing itself, not a written proxy for it.","note":"Backfires when: stretched to mean any practical task. It implies genuine real-world fidelity."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-20","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Spiralled","sense":"revisiting concepts at rising complexity","say":"The curriculum is *spiralled*, so they meet syncopation three times, harder each year.","note":"Backfires when: used for simple repetition. The point is increasing complexity, not return alone."},{"id":"fl-vic-academic-21","register":"Pedagogy","word":"Disposition","sense":"a habitual attitude or way of approaching work","say":"I'm trying to build a *disposition* toward practice, not just teach the pieces.","note":"Backfires when: used vaguely for 'attitude'. It means a settled, trainable habit of mind."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-1","register":"Strategy","word":"Capacity","sense":"the resource or bandwidth available","say":"We don't have the *capacity* to run a fourth ensemble this term.","note":"Backfires when: used to soften a plain 'we can't'. Sometimes the blunt version is stronger."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-2","register":"Strategy","word":"Prioritise","sense":"rank by importance and act accordingly","say":"If we're honest, we have to *prioritise* the showcase over the camp logistics this fortnight.","note":"Backfires when: used as a verb with no actual ranking behind it."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-3","register":"Strategy","word":"Mandate","sense":"the authority to act","say":"I don't have a clear *mandate* to make that call alone – it needs Council.","note":"Backfires when: used to claim authority you're really just asserting. Reserve for genuine remit questions."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-4","register":"Strategy","word":"Contingent","sense":"dependent on something else","say":"The whole plan is *contingent* on getting the relief staff approved.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'depends on' is clearer to the room."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-5","register":"Strategy","word":"Material","sense":"significant enough to affect the outcome","say":"That's a real concern, but it's not *material* to the decision in front of us.","note":"Backfires when: used to wave away something that actually does matter to the person raising it."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-6","register":"Strategy","word":"Remit","sense":"the area you're responsible for","say":"Scheduling sits outside my *remit*, so I'll flag it rather than decide it.","note":"Backfires when: used to dodge ownership of something that is in fact yours."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-7","register":"Strategy","word":"Sustainable","sense":"able to continue without burning out the system","say":"This workload isn't *sustainable*, and I'd rather say so now than in November.","note":"Backfires when: overused as a buzzword. It lands when it names a real limit."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-8","register":"Strategy","word":"Sequence (it)","sense":"order the steps deliberately","say":"Let's *sequence* this properly: staffing first, then repertoire, then the parent email.","note":"Backfires when: used for a two-item list where 'order' would do."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-9","register":"Strategy","word":"Latitude","sense":"room to act at one's discretion","say":"I'd like some *latitude* on how we run the showcase, within the budget you've set.","note":"Backfires when: used to ask for a blank cheque. It works when paired with a clear constraint."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-10","register":"Strategy","word":"Defer","sense":"postpone deliberately, or yield to another","say":"I'd *defer* that decision until we have the enrolment numbers in front of us.","note":"Backfires when: used to avoid a decision that's actually ready to be made."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-11","register":"Strategy","word":"Underwrite","sense":"take on the risk or backing for","say":"I'm willing to *underwrite* the extra rehearsal time out of the program budget.","note":"Backfires when: used loosely for 'support'. It implies you're carrying real risk – mean it."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-12","register":"Strategy","word":"Threshold","sense":"the level that triggers a different response","say":"Below a certain *threshold* of players, the big band isn't viable and we should say so.","note":"Backfires when: stretched to mean any number. Keep it to a genuine trigger point."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-13","register":"Strategy","word":"Discretionary","sense":"within one's own judgement to decide","say":"That spend is *discretionary*, so it's a call I can make without Council.","note":"Backfires when: used to claim authority you don't have. It's a precise budgeting term – be accurate."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-14","register":"Strategy","word":"Bandwidth","sense":"available attention and capacity","say":"I don't have the *bandwidth* to lead a fourth ensemble and do it well.","note":"Backfires when: used as fashionable filler. 'Time' or 'capacity' is often the cleaner word."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-15","register":"Strategy","word":"Front-load","sense":"concentrate effort early","say":"Let's *front-load* the planning this term so the showcase week is calm.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'do early' is plainer. Keep it for genuine effort-weighting."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-16","register":"Strategy","word":"Lever","sense":"a point where small effort yields large effect","say":"The real *lever* here is the timetable, not the budget.","note":"Backfires when: overused as management-speak. It works when you can name the disproportionate effect."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-17","register":"Strategy","word":"Scope","sense":"the agreed boundary of what's included","say":"That's worth doing, but it's outside the *scope* of what we committed to this term.","note":"Backfires when: used to refuse anything inconvenient. It means a real, agreed boundary."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-18","register":"Strategy","word":"Trade-off","sense":"what you give up to gain something else","say":"There's a *trade-off*: more rehearsals means less time for the camp prep.","note":"Backfires when: never, really – naming a trade-off honestly is one of the most mature things you can do."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-19","register":"Strategy","word":"Throughput","sense":"how much gets done per unit of effort","say":"We can lift *throughput* without more hours if we fix the scheduling friction.","note":"Backfires when: applied to people as if they were a process. Keep it for systems and workflow."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-20","register":"Strategy","word":"Headroom","sense":"spare capacity before a limit is hit","say":"We've no *headroom* left in the calendar – anything new displaces something.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'room' would do. It implies a ceiling you're measuring against."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-21","register":"Strategy","word":"Backstop","sense":"a fallback that prevents the worst case","say":"I want a *backstop* in case the relief staff don't come through.","note":"Backfires when: used for any plan B. It specifically means a safeguard against failure, not just an alternative."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-22","register":"Strategy","word":"Cadence","sense":"the rhythm or frequency of recurring work","say":"Let's set a fortnightly *cadence* for these check-ins so nothing drifts.","note":"Backfires when: used as jargon for 'schedule'. It implies a deliberate, sustained rhythm."},{"id":"fl-vic-strategic-23","register":"Strategy","word":"Critical path","sense":"the sequence that determines the deadline","say":"Staffing is on the *critical path* – if it slips, everything after it slips.","note":"Backfires when: used for anything merely important. It means the specific chain that sets the timeline."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-1","register":"Argument","word":"Conflate","sense":"wrongly treat two things as one","say":"I think we're *conflating* attendance with commitment – they're not the same issue.","note":"Backfires when: used to score a point rather than to actually separate two ideas."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-2","register":"Argument","word":"Predicated on","sense":"based on / resting on","say":"That argument is *predicated on* the timetable not changing, which it will.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'based on' carries the same meaning more cleanly."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-3","register":"Argument","word":"Tenable","sense":"able to be defended or held","say":"I don't think that position is *tenable* once parents see the numbers.","note":"Backfires when: deployed to sound clever rather than to genuinely test whether a stance holds."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-4","register":"Argument","word":"Salient","sense":"the most relevant or striking point","say":"The *salient* issue isn't the cost – it's whether we can staff it.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'main' or 'key' is the more natural word for the room."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-5","register":"Argument","word":"Causal","sense":"a genuine cause-and-effect link","say":"We're assuming a *causal* link there, but it might just be coincidence.","note":"Backfires when: used loosely. Reserve it for when you actually mean cause, not correlation."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-6","register":"Argument","word":"Granular","sense":"at a fine level of detail","say":"We don't need to get *granular* in this meeting – let's settle the principle first.","note":"Backfires when: used to avoid detail that the discussion genuinely needs."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-7","register":"Argument","word":"Caveat","sense":"a qualification or condition attached","say":"I'm in favour, with one *caveat*: it has to be reviewed at the end of term.","note":"Backfires when: stacked – one caveat is authority, three is hedging."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-8","register":"Argument","word":"Distinct","sense":"clearly separate","say":"Those are two *distinct* decisions, and I'd like to take them one at a time.","note":"Backfires when: never, really – it's a clean word that slows a muddled discussion down usefully."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-9","register":"Argument","word":"Premise","sense":"the assumption an argument rests on","say":"I'd question the *premise* – we're assuming demand stays flat, and it won't.","note":"Backfires when: used to sound rigorous. Only challenge a premise when you can name the flawed one."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-10","register":"Argument","word":"Spurious","sense":"a connection that looks real but isn't","say":"That correlation looks *spurious* to me – the two probably share a cause.","note":"Backfires when: used as a fancy 'wrong'. It specifically means a false apparent link."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-11","register":"Argument","word":"Proportionate","sense":"matched in scale to the thing it responds to","say":"Is that response *proportionate* to a problem we've seen once?","note":"Backfires when: used to minimise a real issue. It's a fairness test, not a dismissal."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-12","register":"Argument","word":"Contingent on","sense":"true only if something else holds","say":"My support is *contingent on* the review clause staying in.","note":"Backfires when: 'depends on' would be clearer. Use it when you're attaching a firm condition."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-13","register":"Argument","word":"Reductive","sense":"oversimplifying in a way that distorts","say":"That framing is a little *reductive* – there's a third option we're skipping.","note":"Backfires when: used to dismiss a fair simplification. Reserve it for genuine distortion."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-14","register":"Argument","word":"Corollary","sense":"something that follows naturally from","say":"The *corollary* is that we'd also need to fund the extra transport.","note":"Backfires when: used where 'so' or 'which means' is plainer. Keep it for a genuine logical consequence."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-15","register":"Argument","word":"Equivocate","sense":"use vague language to avoid committing","say":"I don't want to *equivocate*, so I'll say plainly: I'm against it.","note":"Backfires when: followed by equivocation. The word sets up directness – then be direct."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-16","register":"Argument","word":"Necessary condition","sense":"required for something, though maybe not enough alone","say":"Funding is a *necessary condition*, but it won't be sufficient on its own.","note":"Backfires when: used loosely. Pairs best with 'not sufficient' to make a precise point."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-17","register":"Argument","word":"Counterfactual","sense":"what would have happened otherwise","say":"The *counterfactual* matters – would attainment have risen anyway, without the change?","note":"Backfires when: used to sound rigorous. Only invoke it when the comparison genuinely bears on the claim."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-18","register":"Argument","word":"Conflate","sense":"wrongly merge two distinct things","say":"We're *conflating* attendance with commitment – they're not the same variable.","note":"Backfires when: used to score a point rather than to actually separate the two ideas."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-19","register":"Argument","word":"Inference","sense":"a conclusion drawn from evidence","say":"That's an *inference*, not an observation – and it's the step I'd question.","note":"Backfires when: used interchangeably with 'guess'. It means a reasoned step, which you should be able to show."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-20","register":"Argument","word":"Confounding variable","sense":"a hidden factor distorting an apparent link","say":"Term length could be the *confounding variable* driving both numbers.","note":"Backfires when: there's no actual data relationship to confound. Reserve it for genuine evidence claims."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-21","register":"Argument","word":"Parsimonious","sense":"the simplest explanation that fits","say":"The more *parsimonious* reading is that they simply weren't told.","note":"Backfires when: used to dismiss complexity that's real. It favours simplicity, not oversimplification."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-22","register":"Argument","word":"Beg the question","sense":"assume the very thing in dispute","say":"That *begs the question* – it assumes the program's the problem, which is what we're testing.","note":"Backfires when: used to mean 'raises the question'. Half the room uses the loose sense; know your audience."},{"id":"fl-vic-analytical-23","register":"Argument","word":"First principles","sense":"reasoning up from basics, not analogy","say":"Let's reason from *first principles* rather than from how it's always been done.","note":"Backfires when: used as a buzzword. It commits you to actually starting from the fundamentals."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-1","register":"University","word":"Collegial","sense":"governance by peers, by deliberation rather than fiat","say":"I'd want this taken through the *collegial* process rather than decided in the executive.","note":"Register: central to university governance – it signals you understand academic decision-making isn't top-down. Misfires only if you invoke it to obstruct a decision that legitimately sits with management."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-2","register":"University","word":"Quorum","sense":"the minimum present for a decision to be valid","say":"Do we have *quorum* to resolve this, or are we minuting it for ratification?","note":"Register: precise and expected. Using it correctly marks you as someone who reads the standing orders."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-3","register":"University","word":"Take it on notice","sense":"formally defer a question for a considered later answer","say":"I'll *take that on notice* and bring a full response to the next meeting.","note":"Register: the senior way to avoid answering badly under pressure without looking evasive. One of the most useful phrases you can own."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-4","register":"University","word":"Ratify","sense":"formally confirm a decision already taken","say":"The sub-committee's done the work; we're here to *ratify*, not reopen it.","note":"Register: deploys well to stop a settled matter being relitigated. Backfires if the decision genuinely wasn't sound – ratification isn't a rubber stamp."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-5","register":"University","word":"Terms of reference","sense":"the formal scope of what a body may consider","say":"That sits outside our *terms of reference* – it's a matter for Academic Board.","note":"Register: the cleanest way to decline a question without declining it personally. Authoritative because it's structural, not preferential."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-6","register":"University","word":"Substantive vs procedural","sense":"the issue itself versus the process around it","say":"Let's separate the *substantive* question from the *procedural* one – they need different conversations.","note":"Register: a hallmark of someone fluent in governance. Lands hard in a room that's confusing the two, which they often are."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-7","register":"University","word":"Devolve","sense":"delegate authority to a lower level","say":"I'd *devolve* the operational detail to the working group and keep the principle here.","note":"Register: precise and senior. Don't use it for simple 'hand off' – it implies a deliberate distribution of authority."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-8","register":"University","word":"In camera","sense":"a session closed to the usual attendees","say":"Can we move *in camera* for this item? It touches on a personnel matter.","note":"Register: correct and expected in formal governance. Using it appropriately signals discretion; using it to hide an ordinary discussion looks like manoeuvring."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-9","register":"University","word":"Cyclical review","sense":"scheduled periodic re-examination, not ad hoc","say":"This belongs in the *cyclical review*, not a one-off change mid-year.","note":"Register: resists reactive decision-making with the weight of process behind it. Strong in any body that does scheduled reviews."},{"id":"fl-vic-university-10","register":"University","word":"Without prejudice","sense":"said without binding a future position","say":"*Without prejudice* to the final decision, here's where my thinking sits today.","note":"Register: lets you think aloud without being held to it. Useful, but overuse signals you never commit to anything."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-1","register":"SCSA","word":"Consensus advice","sense":"SCSA committees advise by consensus, not by vote","say":"We provide *consensus advice* here – I'd rather we land somewhere we can all stand behind than force a split.","note":"Register: this is literally how SCSA advisory committees work. Naming it correctly marks you as someone who knows the room's actual function, not just its topic."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-2","register":"SCSA","word":"Achievement standards","sense":"the defined level of learning expected at each stage","say":"The proposal lifts content without lifting the *achievement standards* to match – that's a mismatch.","note":"Register: core SCSA vocabulary, distinct from 'content'. Conflating the two is the giveaway of someone outside the work; keeping them separate is the mark of someone inside it."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-3","register":"SCSA","word":"Syllabus (vs curriculum)","sense":"the specified course; the Outline is the broader frame","say":"That's a *syllabus*-level change, so it triggers the cyclical review, not a circular.","note":"Register: in WA the distinction is real and procedural. Use the right level and you sound fluent; blur it and you don't."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-4","register":"SCSA","word":"Moderation","sense":"aligning teacher judgements to a common standard","say":"Without consensus *moderation*, we can't claim comparability across schools.","note":"Register: central to assessment integrity in WA. A precise, expected term – comfortable to use freely in this room."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-5","register":"SCSA","word":"Comparability","sense":"that a grade means the same across contexts","say":"The question is whether this preserves *comparability* between metropolitan and remote schools.","note":"Register: a genuine equity concern SCSA takes seriously. Raising it shows you're thinking system-wide, not just about your own school."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-6","register":"SCSA","word":"Cyclical review","sense":"the scheduled rolling review of syllabuses","say":"This is exactly what the *cyclical review* exists to handle – let's not pre-empt it.","note":"Register: SCSA reviews syllabuses on a cycle by design. Invoking it resists reactive change with the authority of established process."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-7","register":"SCSA","word":"Implementation timeline","sense":"the phased rollout schedule for a change","say":"My concern is the *implementation timeline* – schools need lead time for professional learning.","note":"Register: shifts a debate from whether to how-and-when, which is often where the real risk sits. Practical and well-regarded."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-8","register":"SCSA","word":"Fit for purpose","sense":"genuinely suited to its intended use","say":"It's defensible on paper; I'm not convinced it's *fit for purpose* in a small-cohort school.","note":"Register: common and effective, but near-cliché – it lands when paired with the specific context that makes it true, as in the example."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-9","register":"SCSA","word":"Equity of access","sense":"fair availability across all student groups","say":"Does this hold up on *equity of access* for students without instruments at home?","note":"Register: a value SCSA's strategic plan foregrounds. Genuine and expected; hollow only if you raise it without a real access gap in mind."},{"id":"fl-vic-scsa-10","register":"SCSA","word":"Evidence base","sense":"the data and research a decision rests on","say":"What's the *evidence base* for the change? I'd want to see it before we advise on it.","note":"Register: a clean, senior way to slow an under-supported proposal. Almost never backfires in a standards body."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-1","register":"Board","word":"Fiduciary duty","sense":"the legal obligation to act in the body's best interest","say":"We have a *fiduciary duty* here that sits above any one program's interests, including mine.","note":"Register: serious and precise. It signals you understand a board's legal weight. Overusing it for ordinary decisions cheapens it – reserve it for genuine duty-of-care or financial-stewardship moments."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-2","register":"Board","word":"Governance vs operations","sense":"the board sets direction; staff execute it","say":"That's an *operational* matter – we'd be straying from *governance* into management if we decided it here.","note":"Register: the single most useful distinction on any board. Naming it keeps the board out of the weeds and marks you as someone who understands the role."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-3","register":"Board","word":"Risk appetite","sense":"how much risk the body is willing to carry","say":"This turns on our *risk appetite* – are we a board that trials things, or one that waits for certainty?","note":"Register: reframes a yes/no fight into a values question the board can actually own. Sophisticated and disarming."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-4","register":"Board","word":"Materiality","sense":"whether something is significant enough to act on","say":"Is this a question of *materiality*? If the exposure is small, it may not warrant board time.","note":"Register: from audit and finance, but widely understood. Helps a board triage what deserves its attention. Misfires if used to wave off something that genuinely matters to stakeholders."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-5","register":"Board","word":"Stewardship","sense":"responsible care of something held in trust","say":"Our job is *stewardship* of the program for the students who come after this cohort.","note":"Register: warm and weighty at once. Lands well in a values-driven board; reads as grandiose if attached to a trivial item."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-6","register":"Board","word":"Conflict of interest","sense":"a competing personal interest, declared openly","say":"I should declare a *conflict of interest* on this item and step back from the decision.","note":"Register: declaring one proactively is a mark of integrity, not weakness – it builds standing. Given your own role overlaps, this is a genuinely useful one to have ready."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-7","register":"Board","word":"In-principle support","sense":"backing the direction while details are settled","say":"I'd offer *in-principle support*, contingent on seeing the budget before we commit.","note":"Register: lets a board move forward without signing a blank cheque. Precise and constructive."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-8","register":"Board","word":"Defer to the executive","sense":"leave a call to the people who run things day to day","say":"On the staffing detail I'd *defer to the executive* – that's their call to make, not ours.","note":"Register: shows you know the board's limits. Strengthens your standing when you later do hold firm on a genuine governance matter."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-9","register":"Board","word":"On the record","sense":"formally minuted as a stated position","say":"I want it *on the record* that I raised the resourcing risk before we proceeded.","note":"Register: protects you and signals seriousness. Use sparingly – a person who wants everything on the record reads as defensive rather than principled."},{"id":"fl-vic-board-10","register":"Board","word":"Mission alignment","sense":"consistency with the body's core purpose","say":"Before the detail, I'd ask whether this is in *mission alignment* – does it serve why the program exists?","note":"Register: elevates a discussion from logistics to purpose, which is the board's proper altitude. Hollow only if the mission is invoked as a slogan rather than a test."},{"id":"fl-voc-1","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Concretely","sense":"In specific terms","say":"Concretely, that means two extra rehearsals.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-2","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"My read is","sense":"My interpretation","say":"Opens a view with confidence, invites no permission.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-3","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"The crux","sense":"The decisive point","say":"The crux is whether we have the staff.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-4","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Pragmatically","sense":"In practical terms","say":"Cuts through theory to what's actually doable.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-5","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Untenable","sense":"Cannot be sustained","say":"The current timeline is untenable.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-6","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"I'll own","sense":"I take responsibility for","say":"I'll own the parent comms.\" Clean, no hedging.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-7","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"The trade-off","sense":"What we give up to gain","say":"Names a cost honestly. Reads as maturity.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-8","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Material","sense":"Significant enough to matter","say":"That's not a material risk.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-9","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Categorically","sense":"Without exception","say":"I categorically can't approve that.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-10","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Where I land","sense":"My settled position","say":"Where I land is: we wait a term.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-11","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Discrete","sense":"Separate and distinct","say":"Those are two discrete issues.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-12","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Non-negotiable","sense":"Not open to change","say":"Use rarely. It lands hardest when it's scarce.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-13","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"In short","sense":"Signals a crisp summary","say":"In short: we wait a term.\" Forces brevity on yourself.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-14","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Functionally","sense":"In practical effect","say":"Functionally, that's a no.\" Cuts past technicalities.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-15","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"To be precise","sense":"Flags an exact correction","say":"To be precise, it's three students, not the year group.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-16","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"The substance","sense":"The real matter, not the form","say":"On the substance, I agree.\" Separates issue from process.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-17","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Net","sense":"After everything's weighed","say":"Net, it costs us a fortnight.\" Compresses a calculation.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-18","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Squarely","sense":"Directly and unambiguously","say":"That sits squarely with the executive.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-19","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"On balance","sense":"Weighing it all up","say":"On balance, I'd proceed.\" Signals you've considered both sides.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-20","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Demonstrably","sense":"Provably, with evidence","say":"That's demonstrably not working.\" Stronger than 'clearly'.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-21","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Tellingly","sense":"In a way that reveals something","say":"Tellingly, no one's volunteered to run it.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-22","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"Plainly","sense":"Without hedging","say":"Plainly, the timeline won't hold.","note":""},{"id":"fl-voc-23","register":"Quick vocabulary","word":"At root","sense":"At the fundamental level","say":"At root, this is a staffing problem.","note":""}],"registerNotes":{"Committee moves":"This is a phrasing move for taking or holding the floor in any committee – the value is in the structure of the sentence, not a single word.","Rhetorical moves":"This is a rhetorical manoeuvre. Its power is structural: it works by how it positions you relative to the argument, and it collapses the moment it's done in bad faith.","High register":"This is a high-register term. At your level the skill isn't knowing it – it's judging which room takes it and which finds it affected. The register note is the part that matters most.","Pedagogy":"Pedagogical vocabulary. It earns its place when paired with a concrete example of the practice; dropped as a bare label, an experienced educator will test whether you mean it.","Strategy":"Leadership and planning vocabulary. It reads as command when it names something precise, and as management-speak when it's reaching for weight it hasn't earned.","Argument":"Argument vocabulary. These words sharpen reasoning, so they only land if the reasoning underneath them is actually sound – they advertise rigour and then have to deliver it.","University":"University governance language. Used correctly, it signals you understand academic decision-making isn't top-down – that it runs on process, scope, and collegial deliberation.","SCSA":"SCSA / curriculum-standards language. The distinctions here are real and procedural in WA; keeping them precise is what marks you as inside the work rather than outside it.","Board":"Board governance language. The recurring theme is altitude – staying at the level of direction, risk, and duty rather than dropping into operational detail that isn't the board's to decide."},"diction":{"endings":[{"id":"fl-de-1","pair":"fact / fast","tip":"land the hard T and the ST cluster separately"},{"id":"fl-de-2","pair":"strict standards","tip":"two consonant clusters back to back – don't drop the first T"},{"id":"fl-de-3","pair":"correct context","tip":"finish the T on 'correct' before the K of 'context'"},{"id":"fl-de-4","pair":"distinct decision","tip":"the NCT is where it slurs – separate the sounds"},{"id":"fl-de-5","pair":"exact extent","tip":"both end and begin on hard stops; keep them clean"},{"id":"fl-de-6","pair":"draft framework","tip":"the FT then FR is a trap; slow through it"},{"id":"fl-de-7","pair":"asked, acknowledged","tip":"the SKT and the CKN both want to collapse"},{"id":"fl-de-8","pair":"budget constraints","tip":"land the T on budget, then the STR cluster"},{"id":"fl-de-9","pair":"prompt response","tip":"MPT is three consonants – give each its moment"},{"id":"fl-de-10","pair":"strict protocols","tip":"two hard clusters; over-articulate both"},{"id":"fl-de-11","pair":"abrupt transition","tip":"the PT then TR is a pile-up – give it room"},{"id":"fl-de-12","pair":"adjacent districts","tip":"the JCNT and STR clusters both want to flatten"},{"id":"fl-de-13","pair":"prompt prompt","tip":"say it twice; the MPT must stay intact each time"},{"id":"fl-de-14","pair":"crisp consonants","tip":"the SP then hard C – don't let the S bleed in"},{"id":"fl-de-15","pair":"twelfths","tip":"one syllable, five consonants; the hardest word in English to say cleanly"},{"id":"fl-de-16","pair":"sixths and fifths","tip":"the XTH and FTH endings; tongue tip stays busy"},{"id":"fl-de-17","pair":"acts, facts, pacts","tip":"the KTS cluster three times – keep the T audible"},{"id":"fl-de-18","pair":"breadth and depth","tip":"DTH then PTH; finish the TH, don't swallow it"},{"id":"fl-de-19","pair":"strengths","tip":"NGTHS – the consonant marathon; slow right down"},{"id":"fl-de-20","pair":"clasped, grasped","tip":"the SPT ending twice; the P must survive between S and T"},{"id":"fl-de-21","pair":"glimpsed","tip":"MPST – five consonants, one syllable; a genuine summit word"},{"id":"fl-de-22","pair":"texts, contexts","tip":"KSTS cluster; the second S tends to eat the first T"},{"id":"fl-de-23","pair":"insists, persists","tip":"the STS ending; keep the medial T from vanishing"},{"id":"fl-de-24","pair":"hard-pressed budget","tip":"the DPR then ST then DG – three traps in a row"},{"id":"fl-de-25","pair":"correct conduct","tip":"two KT-adjacent words; finish each before the next"},{"id":"fl-de-26","pair":"apt, adept, adopt","tip":"PT and DPT endings; the stop must be heard, not implied"},{"id":"fl-de-27","pair":"facts, tracts, pacts","tip":"KTS three times; the rhythm exposes any dropped T"},{"id":"fl-de-28","pair":"asterisks","tip":"SKS ending; notoriously slurred to 'asterix' – keep all three"},{"id":"fl-de-29","pair":"sixths","tip":"KSTHS; tongue travels far and fast, slow it down"},{"id":"fl-de-30","pair":"prompts, tempts","tip":"MPTS cluster twice; the P is the first casualty"},{"id":"fl-de-31","pair":"sculpts, sculpts","tip":"LPTS ending; four consonants after the vowel"},{"id":"fl-de-32","pair":"depths, widths","tip":"PTHS and DTHS; finish the TH, don't trail off"},{"id":"fl-de-33","pair":"acts strictly","tip":"KTS then STR; two clusters colliding mid-phrase"},{"id":"fl-de-34","pair":"next steps","tip":"KST then ST; the shared S wants to merge them"},{"id":"fl-de-35","pair":"worlds, worlds","tip":"RLDZ; the L and D both want to drop after the R"},{"id":"fl-de-36","pair":"bulbs, films","tip":"LBZ and LMZ; the L must stay before the final consonant"},{"id":"fl-de-37","pair":"ghosts, hosts, posts","tip":"STS ending three times; keep the medial T audible each time"},{"id":"fl-de-38","pair":"crisps, wisps","tip":"SPS ending; the P survives between two S sounds"},{"id":"fl-de-39","pair":"twelfths, fifths","tip":"the two hardest in English back to back; the deep end of endings"}],"multi":[{"id":"fl-dm-1","word":"comparability","syl":"com · pa · ra · bil · i · ty","tip":"the middle 'ra-bil' is where it dies"},{"id":"fl-dm-2","word":"implementation","syl":"im · ple · men · ta · tion","tip":"don't swallow the 'men'"},{"id":"fl-dm-3","word":"responsibility","syl":"re · spon · si · bil · i · ty","tip":"six beats; keep every one"},{"id":"fl-dm-4","word":"substantive","syl":"sub · stan · tive","tip":"the STAN is stressed – land it"},{"id":"fl-dm-5","word":"particularly","syl":"par · tic · u · lar · ly","tip":"the classic slur word; never 'particuly'"},{"id":"fl-dm-6","word":"infrastructure","syl":"in · fra · struc · ture","tip":"the FRA-STRUC pile-up needs space"},{"id":"fl-dm-7","word":"prioritisation","syl":"pri · or · i · ti · sa · tion","tip":"a marathon; slow all the way through"},{"id":"fl-dm-8","word":"differentiation","syl":"dif · fer · en · ti · a · tion","tip":"the 'en-ti-a' is the collapse point"},{"id":"fl-dm-9","word":"accountability","syl":"ac · coun · ta · bil · i · ty","tip":"hard C up front, then keep pace"},{"id":"fl-dm-10","word":"statutory","syl":"stat · u · tory","tip":"the double T wants to vanish – keep it"},{"id":"fl-dm-11","word":"hierarchical","syl":"hi · er · ar · chi · cal","tip":"five beats people rush into three"},{"id":"fl-dm-12","word":"reconciliation","syl":"re · con · cil · i · a · tion","tip":"the 'cil-i-a' string needs deliberate space"},{"id":"fl-dm-13","word":"institutional","syl":"in · sti · tu · tion · al","tip":"the STI-TU is where it slurs"},{"id":"fl-dm-14","word":"unequivocally","syl":"un · e · quiv · o · cal · ly","tip":"six beats; the QUIV is the pivot – land it"},{"id":"fl-dm-15","word":"jurisdiction","syl":"ju · ris · dic · tion","tip":"the RIS-DIC must stay crisp, not 'jurisdiction' run flat"},{"id":"fl-dm-16","word":"preliminary","syl":"pre · lim · i · nar · y","tip":"don't drop to 'preliminry' – keep the 'i-nar'"},{"id":"fl-dm-17","word":"contemporaneous","syl":"con · tem · po · ra · ne · ous","tip":"a genuine mouthful; six beats, no shortcuts"},{"id":"fl-dm-18","word":"disproportionate","syl":"dis · pro · por · tion · ate","tip":"two 'por' sounds close together; keep them distinct"},{"id":"fl-dm-19","word":"methodological","syl":"meth · o · do · log · i · cal","tip":"the 'do-log' middle is the collapse zone"},{"id":"fl-dm-20","word":"interdisciplinary","syl":"in · ter · dis · ci · plin · ar · y","tip":"seven beats – the longest in the set; pace it like a slow scale"},{"id":"fl-dm-21","word":"corroborate","syl":"cor · rob · o · rate","tip":"the double R then B; don't let it become 'collaborate'"},{"id":"fl-dm-22","word":"exemplary","syl":"ex · em · pla · ry","tip":"stress the EM; people rush it to three beats"},{"id":"fl-dm-23","word":"ameliorate","syl":"a · mel · io · rate","tip":"the 'mel-io' needs separation or it mushes"},{"id":"fl-dm-24","word":"phenomenological","syl":"phe · nom · e · no · log · i · cal","tip":"seven beats; an academic-room staple, drill it cold"},{"id":"fl-dm-25","word":"epistemological","syl":"e · pis · te · mo · log · i · cal","tip":"the 'pis-te-mo' run is the danger; pace it evenly"},{"id":"fl-dm-26","word":"particularity","syl":"par · tic · u · lar · i · ty","tip":"don't let it shrink to 'particularty'"},{"id":"fl-dm-27","word":"incontrovertible","syl":"in · con · tro · vert · i · ble","tip":"the 'tro-vert' pivot carries the stress"},{"id":"fl-dm-28","word":"indispensable","syl":"in · dis · pen · sa · ble","tip":"keep the 'pen-sa' from collapsing into one beat"},{"id":"fl-dm-29","word":"quintessential","syl":"quin · tes · sen · tial","tip":"two sibilants close together; keep them distinct"},{"id":"fl-dm-30","word":"deterioration","syl":"de · te · ri · o · ra · tion","tip":"six beats, four of them vowels; don't let them smear"},{"id":"fl-dm-31","word":"proliferation","syl":"pro · lif · er · a · tion","tip":"the 'lif-er-a' middle is the slur zone"},{"id":"fl-dm-32","word":"juxtaposition","syl":"jux · ta · po · si · tion","tip":"the JUXT cluster up front is the hard part"},{"id":"fl-dm-33","word":"verisimilitude","syl":"ver · i · si · mil · i · tude","tip":"six beats; a showpiece word, master it slowly"},{"id":"fl-dm-34","word":"circumlocution","syl":"cir · cum · lo · cu · tion","tip":"ironically, a word for waffle; say it crisply to prove the point"},{"id":"fl-dm-35","word":"idiosyncratic","syl":"id · i · o · syn · crat · ic","tip":"the 'i-o-syn' vowel run then the hard CRAT; pace it"},{"id":"fl-dm-36","word":"unprecedented","syl":"un · prec · e · dent · ed","tip":"don't drop to 'unpresidented'; the C is soft but present"},{"id":"fl-dm-37","word":"prerogative","syl":"pre · rog · a · tive","tip":"the first R is real; not 'perogative'"},{"id":"fl-dm-38","word":"deteriorate","syl":"de · te · ri · o · rate","tip":"four near-vowels in a row; keep them from smearing"},{"id":"fl-dm-39","word":"hypothetical","syl":"hy · po · thet · i · cal","tip":"the THET is the stress anchor; land it"},{"id":"fl-dm-40","word":"parliamentary","syl":"par · lia · men · ta · ry","tip":"the 'lia' is two beats people fuse into one"},{"id":"fl-dm-41","word":"bureaucratic","syl":"bu · reau · crat · ic","tip":"the 'reau' then hard CRAT; don't rush the join"},{"id":"fl-dm-42","word":"conscientious","syl":"con · sci · en · tious","tip":"two SH-adjacent sounds; keep the 'sci-en' distinct"},{"id":"fl-dm-43","word":"susceptibility","syl":"sus · cep · ti · bil · i · ty","tip":"the SUS-CEP start is the slur point; six beats total"},{"id":"fl-dm-44","word":"extemporaneous","syl":"ex · tem · po · ra · ne · ous","tip":"six beats; fittingly, the word for unrehearsed speech needs rehearsal"},{"id":"fl-dm-45","word":"perspicacious","syl":"per · spi · ca · cious","tip":"the PER-SPI cluster up front; a showpiece, drill cold"},{"id":"fl-dm-46","word":"magnanimous","syl":"mag · nan · i · mous","tip":"the double 'nan-i' middle wants to collapse"},{"id":"fl-dm-47","word":"obsequious","syl":"ob · se · qui · ous","tip":"the QUI is a full beat; not 'obseqous'"}],"sentences":[{"id":"fl-ds-1","text":"The *d*raft *f*ramework *d*oesn't *r*eflect the *c*orrect *c*ontext.","note":"D and F and hard C work – clean stops throughout."},{"id":"fl-ds-2","text":"*S*trict *s*tandards *s*hould *s*till *s*tand.","note":"five S onsets; keep each crisp, don't let them blur into one hiss."},{"id":"fl-ds-3","text":"We *p*rompted a *p*roper, *p*recise, *p*ragmatic *p*roposal.","note":"plosive P drill – pop each one."},{"id":"fl-ds-4","text":"*Th*e *th*ree *th*orough *th*resholds *th*at *th*ey *s*et.","note":"TH against S – the two get confused under speed."},{"id":"fl-ds-5","text":"*C*ritical *c*urriculum *c*hanges *c*ome *c*autiously.","note":"hard C onsets; resist softening to G."},{"id":"fl-ds-6","text":"*B*oard *b*usiness *b*rooks no *b*lurred *b*oundaries.","note":"voiced B drill – full lip closure each time."},{"id":"fl-ds-7","text":"*L*argely *l*ogical, *l*argely *l*ucid, *l*argely *l*anded.","note":"the L is where tired tongues go lazy; keep the tip active."},{"id":"fl-ds-8","text":"*R*igorous *r*eview *r*equires *r*eal *r*easoning.","note":"R onsets without a vowel run-up; clean attack."},{"id":"fl-ds-9","text":"*G*enuine *g*overnance *g*uards *g*ood *g*roundwork.","note":"voiced G; don't let it soften toward a K."},{"id":"fl-ds-10","text":"*Th*ese *th*orough, *th*oughtful *th*eses *th*rive.","note":"voiced and unvoiced TH mixed; feel the difference on your tongue."},{"id":"fl-ds-11","text":"*F*ive *f*ine *f*ull *f*rameworks *f*ailed *f*ast.","note":"F is a top-teeth-to-lip sound; keep it from drifting to a V."},{"id":"fl-ds-12","text":"*D*eliberate, *d*etailed, *d*ecisive *d*ialogue.","note":"hard D onsets; tongue tip to the ridge each time."},{"id":"fl-ds-13","text":"*W*e *w*illingly *w*eigh *w*hat *w*orks.","note":"rounded W; don't let it collapse into the next vowel."},{"id":"fl-ds-14","text":"*N*ine *n*uanced *n*otions *n*eed *n*aming.","note":"N stays forward; resist nasalising the whole phrase."},{"id":"fl-ds-15","text":"*K*een *c*ommittees *k*eep *c*lear *c*onclusions.","note":"hard K and C; pop the back of the tongue cleanly."},{"id":"fl-ds-16","text":"*P*roper *p*lanning *p*revents *p*oor *p*erformance.","note":"the classic P drill; a small puff of air on each."},{"id":"fl-ds-17","text":"*S*even *s*ensible *s*chools *s*ought *s*upport.","note":"S without slipping to SH; keep the hiss tight and short."},{"id":"fl-ds-18","text":"*B*oth *b*oards *b*roadly *b*acked the *b*rief.","note":"voiced B with full lip closure; don't let 'broadly' soften."},{"id":"fl-ds-19","text":"*V*arious *v*iable *v*entures *v*anished.","note":"V is voiced F; feel the buzz on the lip, distinct from F."},{"id":"fl-ds-20","text":"*Ch*oose *ch*allenging *ch*anges *ch*eerfully.","note":"the CH affricate; a clean T-then-SH, not a mushy J."},{"id":"fl-ds-21","text":"*J*udges *j*udged *j*argon *j*ustly.","note":"voiced J against the unvoiced CH above; alternate the two."},{"id":"fl-ds-22","text":"*M*any *m*ore *m*embers *m*ust *m*eet.","note":"M with full closure; resist humming through the phrase."},{"id":"fl-ds-23","text":"*Qu*ite *qu*ick *qu*estions *qu*ieten *qu*arrels.","note":"the KW onset; both sounds present, not just 'kw' smeared."},{"id":"fl-ds-24","text":"*Sh*e *sh*ould *sh*ow *sh*arper *sh*ape.","note":"SH held just long enough; don't clip it to S."},{"id":"fl-ds-25","text":"*Thr*ee *thr*illing *thr*ust *thr*oughout.","note":"THR is three articulations stacked; the hardest onset cluster."},{"id":"fl-ds-26","text":"*Spl*endid *spr*awling *str*uctures *scr*aped through.","note":"four three-consonant onsets; the deep end of attack drills."}],"lines":[{"id":"fl-dl-1","text":"That sits *outside* our *terms of reference*.","note":"the 'outside our' wants to elide – keep the D and the vowel separate."},{"id":"fl-dl-2","text":"I'd want *comparability* preserved across *contexts*.","note":"the trap word in a real sentence; don't rush to recover after it."},{"id":"fl-dl-3","text":"This is a *substantive* matter, not a *procedural* one.","note":"two long words in one breath; land both fully or the contrast is lost."},{"id":"fl-dl-4","text":"I'll *take that on notice* and *respond* at the next meeting.","note":"crisp the T's; 'take that' is where it mushes."},{"id":"fl-dl-5","text":"My support is *in-principle*, *contingent* on the *budget*.","note":"three precise terms; the NT in contingent is the slur point."},{"id":"fl-dl-6","text":"We have a *fiduciary* *duty* that *outranks* any one *interest*.","note":"'fiduciary' is four beats – fi-du-ci-ary; don't collapse to three."},{"id":"fl-dl-7","text":"Let's not *conflate* *implementation* with *intent*.","note":"two big words plus the hard T endings; slow right down."},{"id":"fl-dl-8","text":"I'd *defer* to the *executive* on the *operational* detail.","note":"'executive' and 'operational' back to back is the real test; pace it."},{"id":"fl-dl-9","text":"That falls within our *jurisdiction*, not the *executive's*.","note":"two heavy words; the JCT in jurisdiction is the slur point."},{"id":"fl-dl-10","text":"I'd want this *corroborated* before we *ratify* it.","note":"don't let 'corroborated' become 'collaborated'; land the B."},{"id":"fl-dl-11","text":"The *methodology* is sound; the *implementation* worries me.","note":"two five-beat words in one breath; slow through both."},{"id":"fl-dl-12","text":"This is a *disproportionate* response to a *preliminary* finding.","note":"both words collapse easily; keep every syllable."},{"id":"fl-dl-13","text":"I'd call that *unequivocally* outside our *remit*.","note":"'unequivocally' is the centrepiece – six beats, no rush."},{"id":"fl-dl-14","text":"An *interdisciplinary* approach needs *institutional* backing.","note":"the two longest words in the bank, side by side; this is the summit drill."},{"id":"fl-dl-15","text":"Let's *ameliorate* the risk before it becomes *material*.","note":"'ameliorate' is unfamiliar in the mouth; rehearse it alone first."},{"id":"fl-dl-16","text":"That argument is *incontrovertible* on the *evidence*.","note":"land all five beats of 'incontrovertible'; don't rush to 'evidence'."},{"id":"fl-dl-17","text":"This is the *quintessential* *jurisdiction* question.","note":"two sibilant-heavy words; keep each distinct, don't blur the S sounds."},{"id":"fl-dl-18","text":"I'd resist the *proliferation* of *sub-committees*.","note":"the 'lif-er-a' run then the SUB-COM stop; pace both."},{"id":"fl-dl-19","text":"Our *accountability* is *indispensable* to *stewardship*.","note":"three long words in one sentence; this is an endurance line."},{"id":"fl-dl-20","text":"The *juxtaposition* of *policy* and *practice* is telling.","note":"the JUXT onset is the hurdle; the rest is rhythm."},{"id":"fl-dl-21","text":"I'd avoid *circumlocution* and state it *plainly*.","note":"say the long word crisply, then drop into the short clean one – the contrast is the point."},{"id":"fl-dl-22","text":"That reflects a *phenomenological*, not *empirical*, view.","note":"seven beats then four; an academic-register summit line, drill slowly."}]},"twisters":[{"id":"fl-tw-1","text":"Red leather, yellow leather.","tip":"slow then fast, three times"},{"id":"fl-tw-2","text":"Unique New York, you need New York.","tip":"crisp the N and Y"},{"id":"fl-tw-3","text":"The lips, the teeth, the tip of the tongue.","tip":"over-articulate"},{"id":"fl-tw-4","text":"A proper copper coffee pot.","tip":"pop the P and hard C"},{"id":"fl-tw-5","text":"Selfish shellfish, six slick slim sycamore saplings.","tip":"do not rush the S clusters"},{"id":"fl-tw-6","text":"Three free throws, thrice.","tip":"separate the TH and FR"},{"id":"fl-tw-7","text":"Particularly, regularly, peculiarly.","tip":"every syllable lands"}],"resonance":[{"line":"Hum a low, comfortable note. Feel it in your sternum, not your nose.","note":"Then open the hum into \"maaah\" without raising the pitch. That is your grounded speaking register, lower and slower than you think."},{"line":"\"One. Two. Three.\" Drop the pitch a step on each number.","note":"Trains the downward inflection that reads as certainty. Statements end down, not up."},{"line":"Count to five on a single breath, slowing as you go. Then to eight.","note":"Builds the breath capacity that stops you running out mid-sentence, which is where the stutter lives."}],"breath":[{"name":"Settle","pattern":[4,4,6,0]},{"name":"Box","pattern":[4,4,4,4]},{"name":"Pre-meeting","pattern":[5,2,7,0]}],"routine":[{"t":"Low breathing","d":"One round on the Settle pattern. Hand on stomach. Drop your shoulders.","time":"60 sec"},{"t":"Tongue twisters","d":"Two of them, slow then fast. Wake the articulators up.","time":"45 sec"},{"t":"Find the chest","d":"Hum low, open to 'maaah'. Locate your grounded register and stay there.","time":"30 sec"},{"t":"Three directness drills","d":"Read aloud. Land the bold word. Hold the silence after the full stop.","time":"90 sec"},{"t":"One phrasebook swap","d":"Pick the context you're walking into. Say the strong version five times.","time":"60 sec"},{"t":"Two diction words","d":"From Diction & Clarity, pick two multisyllabic words. Say each by its beats, then at speed.","time":"40 sec"},{"t":"One spoken intervention","d":"From Speaking Practice, choose one for the room you're walking into. Say it aloud twice – land the words, hold the pauses.","time":"60 sec"}]};
